    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.5,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.05,
    "rationale": "The sudden plateau at about 0.5 from 5 h onward could have meant the reader was saturating, so I tested whether readings scale with dilution. The 18 h aliquot diluted 10x read 0.0513 and 0.0506 (×10 gives about 0.51). Diluted 2x, it read 0.244 and 0.2456 (×2 gives about 0.49). Both match the undiluted 0.49. The 14 h aliquot diluted 5x read 0.1053 and 0.0854 (×5 gives about 0.48), close to the undiluted 0.49. The reader is proportional from about 0.05 to 0.5, so the plateau is a real stationary phase, not a reader ceiling. Late biomass is about OD600 0.5, as the undiluted readings show."
  },
